      "writtenOn": "2021-10-20T00:21:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My understanding of this design has always been that the GSCVD requirement would be hardcoded (based on board ID). This approach does not seem safe. If an attacker can manage to erase the cache (e.g. by triggering a cache update by installing a valid new firmware image and then cutting power at just the right moment), they can circumvent the protection.",
      "revId": "e0d208b889455c5c43ca078a56bbeff417375101",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a161c15a_b2a7570e",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000039
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-20T01:09:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this is a good point, the intention was to allow older boards to update to new RO versions with RO_GSCVD areas present.\n\nMaintaining an ever growing list of included board IDs does not seem practical. We can add another indicator of the impending cache erase/update, this way even if power is interrupted after erase before the update we\u0027d know that this device is supposed to run verification.\n\nLet\u0027s discuss this further on the tracker.",
      "parentUuid": "58233dc2_64c73c71",
      "revId": "e0d208b889455c5c43ca078a56bbeff417375101",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fbafb639_40af106b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002133
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-10-21T23:36:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m pretty sure we have no interest in updating RO_GSCVD sections to boards that didn\u0027t originally ship with them. That\u0027s just way too complicated and too big of a change to be worth it for stable boards. There\u0027s no major use case where RO firmware gets updated after a board ships anyway (it\u0027s not worth adding this feature just to the few devices that go through RMA).\n\n\u003e Maintaining an ever growing list of included board IDs does not seem practical.\n\nPresumably the list would only need to grow until the point where we switch to Dauntless/OT... at that point, every board supported by those chips would use this scheme (in the full RO verification with WP monitoring version). So hopefully the handful of boards we\u0027re still going to newly ship before that could fit in a hardcoded list without too much trouble?",
      "parentUuid": "a161c15a_b2a7570e",
      "revId": "e0d208b889455c5c43ca078a56bbeff417375101",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "27ca79ac_5cda539b",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
